---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';import ResourceLibrary from '../components/ResourceLibrary';import {sources} from '../lib/catalog';
---
<Layout title="Resources" active="Resources"><div class="page-top"><h1>Good sources. Less searching.</h1><p>The references behind the study guides, with current rules first. Use the lessons to learn the tested ideas; come here when you want to explore further.</p></div><section class="stage-panel" style="margin-bottom:30px;max-width:850px"><h2>Looking for official practice tests?</h2><p>Sign in to FBLA CONNECT and open <strong>More → Courses</strong>. Sample role plays and production tasks are in preparation resources. These materials require a member or adviser account; ask your adviser to activate yours.</p><a href="https://support.fbla.org/hc/en-us/articles/4416902542996-Competition-Prep-Sample-Objective-Tests-Role-Plays-Production-Tests-and-Case-Competitions" class="plain-link" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FBLA’s access instructions ↗</a></section><section class="archive-directory-intro"><h2>Looking for the Google Drive materials?</h2><p>Browse all 274 original files by competition and material type. Same-title copies and formats are grouped; older rules remain labeled historical.</p><a href="/resources/archive/" class="plain-link">Explore the organized Drive archive →</a></section><ResourceLibrary client:load sources={sources}/><section class="prose" style="margin-top:45px"><h2>How we use these sources</h2><p>Study explanations and practice questions are independently authored. Current Maryland guides set district requirements; national guides set NLC requirements. Public educational resources help explain the concepts. Sources can change, so check the official guide before submitting work.</p><p>Historical Drive materials are optional practice references. They include duplicates and older event names, and their accuracy and reuse rights have not been established. We link to originals rather than republishing that collection.</p><p>We do not claim that reading a guide guarantees a placement or that a short quiz measures the full event. Report conflicting requirements to your adviser and compare the original documents.</p></section></Layout>

